# Build-context allowlist for the OFFLINE GENERATION JOB image.
#
# Separate from `gcloudignore` beside it, which is the SERVING image's context
# and admits only `pilot_backend/` and `pilot_runtime/`. That file is not
# modified by this slice: the served image's build context stays as narrow as
# it was.
#
# This context additionally admits three paths under `genex-parent/`, and only
# three. Without an ignore file at all, `gcloud builds submit` would upload the
# whole repository — several GB of PDFs, notebooks, a tarball, the Parent 2.3
# service and the therapist service — into a build that has no business seeing
# any of it.
#
# Ignore everything, then re-admit exactly what Dockerfile.generation copies.

*

!pilot_backend/
!pilot_backend/**
!pilot_runtime/
!pilot_runtime/**

# The Parent subset the canonical-rung bridge reads. `api/` and `webapp/` are
# NOT admitted: the Parent FastAPI service and frontend are not part of this
# job, and keeping them out of the context keeps them out of a reviewable
# artifact even by accident.
!genex-parent/
!genex-parent/parent_taxonomy/
!genex-parent/parent_taxonomy/**
!genex-parent/genex_core/
!genex-parent/genex_core/**

# Only the parent_2_4 data directory, which holds the two workbooks the
# generation path was measured to open. The other workbooks at the data root —
# including the immutable c2b6735d provenance snapshot — are not read by this
# job and stay out.
!genex-parent/data/
!genex-parent/data/parent_2_4/
!genex-parent/data/parent_2_4/**

# Tests are deleted in the image anyway; keeping them out of the context too
# means they are never uploaded.
pilot_backend/tests/**
pilot_runtime/tests/**
genex-parent/genex_core/tests/**
**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
